_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-02-15T08:31:24Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T17:43:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nThese graphical glitches are reproducible in 4.2 stable and 4.3 stable on the latest patches for each.\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable - Android - Vulkan (Mobile) - integrated Adreno (TM) 650 -  (8 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf you populate a multimeshinstance3d, then modify the instance count, graphical glitches appear in the editor.\n\n<!-- Failed to upload \"Screenrecorder-2025-02-15-10-15-56-170.mp4\" -->\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nStep 1: Create a new project in Mobile rendering device setting.\nStep 2: Create a scene with a Node3D as the root.\nStep 3: Create 1 MultiMeshInstance3D and 2 MeshInstance3Ds as children to the Node3D\nStep 4: Add a mesh to both mesh instances (I used a capsule mesh)\nStep 5. Populate the multimesh. Make the target surface the first mesh, and the source mesh the second mesh.\nStep 6: Change the instance count property in the editor. \nNow, you will see weird graphical glitches in the 3d editor. Some of which may lead to huge lag and crashing\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18809369/test.zip)\nPlease use a mobile device","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102886/reactions","total_